1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,431
In Vanuatu, men tie vines to their
ankles and jump off a wooden tower.

2
00:00:04,951 --> 00:00:08,072
It is a harvest ritual, and it gave
the world bungee jumping.

3
00:00:08,592 --> 00:00:11,933
But the strangest thing about
this country is not the jump.

4
00:00:12,453 --> 00:00:13,653
This is Vanuatu.

5
00:00:13,673 --> 00:00:15,789
The name means land eternal.

6
00:00:16,309 --> 00:00:20,279
It has 83 islands in the South
Pacific, about 335,000 people,

7
00:00:20,299 --> 00:00:22,307
and a capital called Port Vila.

8
00:00:22,827 --> 00:00:25,056
First, a volcano you can walk up to.

9
00:00:25,076 --> 00:00:27,306
Mount Yasur, on the island of Tanna,

10
00:00:27,326 --> 00:00:30,680
is called the most accessible
active volcano on Earth.

11
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:34,724
Four-wheel drives reach about
150 meters from the crater rim,

12
00:00:34,744 --> 00:00:37,570
and visitors watch lava
burst into the night sky.

13
00:00:38,090 --> 00:00:42,845
Captain Cook reported its eruptions
in 1774, and when the alert level climbs,

14
00:00:42,865 --> 00:00:44,271
visitors are kept away.

15
00:00:44,791 --> 00:00:49,750
On the island of Santo, Champagne Beach has white sand that squeaks under your feet.

16
00:00:50,270 --> 00:00:51,897
Nearby, at Million Dollar Point,

17
00:00:51,917 --> 00:00:55,294
the American army pushed its equipment
into the sea after the war,

18
00:00:55,314 --> 00:00:56,632
instead of taking it home.

19
00:00:57,152 --> 00:01:00,257
Today, snorkelers swim over
coral-covered machines.

20
00:01:00,777 --> 00:01:04,581
And inland, blue holes: clear
pools fed by underground rivers.

21
00:01:05,101 --> 00:01:05,891
Now, culture.

22
00:01:05,911 --> 00:01:09,565
Life here runs on kastom,
the word for traditional culture,

23
00:01:09,585 --> 00:01:11,807
from religion to art to the economy.

24
00:01:12,327 --> 00:01:16,791
At its center is the nakamal,
a meeting place under banyan trees.

25
00:01:16,811 --> 00:01:19,758
In town, it is also
the name of a kava bar.

26
00:01:20,278 --> 00:01:24,606
Kava comes from the root of a pepper plant, pounded and strained into an earthy,

27
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:27,649
slightly sedating drink,
served in a half coconut shell.

28
00:01:28,169 --> 00:01:29,187
You drink it in quiet.

29
00:01:29,707 --> 00:01:33,944
The national dish is lap lap, a pudding
of grated roots and coconut milk,

30
00:01:33,964 --> 00:01:36,977
wrapped in banana leaves
and baked under hot stones.

31
00:01:37,497 --> 00:01:42,134
The country has 113 languages,
and artists trace stories in the sand,

32
00:01:42,154 --> 00:01:44,159
an art that UNESCO recognizes.

33
00:01:44,679 --> 00:01:46,508
So what does $10 get you?

34
00:01:46,528 --> 00:01:47,766
About 1,200 vatu.

35
00:01:48,286 --> 00:01:53,053
A bus ride in Port Vila costs about 150 vatu, and a market meal is around 600 vatu.

36
00:01:53,573 --> 00:01:56,805
Add a couple of shells
of kava, and that is $10.

37
00:01:56,825 --> 00:02:01,277
Mount Yasur costs far more, 10,000
vatu or higher, with transport.

38
00:02:01,797 --> 00:02:02,903
Now, the don't list.

39
00:02:03,423 --> 00:02:05,659
Don't walk through a village in swimwear.

40
00:02:05,679 --> 00:02:07,365
Cover your shoulders and knees.

41
00:02:07,885 --> 00:02:11,326
Don't photograph people without
asking, or you may be asked to pay.

42
00:02:11,846 --> 00:02:16,076
Don't step onto a tabu site,
or someone's land, without permission.

43
00:02:16,096 --> 00:02:17,345
Expect a custom fee.

44
00:02:17,865 --> 00:02:20,516
Don't treat a nakamal like a loud bar.

45
00:02:20,536 --> 00:02:24,875
Kava is drunk in quiet, and some
nakamals are closed to women.

46
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:27,785
And don't board just any boat or minibus.

47
00:02:27,805 --> 00:02:31,664
Canada warns that boats between
islands may lack safety equipment,

48
00:02:31,684 --> 00:02:34,132
and minibuses are often in poor condition.

49
00:02:34,652 --> 00:02:39,187
And now, the chapter you were all
waiting for: legends and mysteries.

50
00:02:39,707 --> 00:02:41,822
Legend one, the first dive.

51
00:02:41,842 --> 00:02:50,204
A chief told David Attenborough in 1959 that it began with a woman who had been unfaithful to her husband.

52
00:02:50,724 --> 00:02:55,316
She climbed a tree to escape him, tied vines to her ankles, and jumped. She survived.

53
00:02:55,336 --> 00:02:57,812
Her husband followed,
without vines, and died.

54
00:02:58,332 --> 00:03:03,543
The men, humiliated at being tricked,
built a tower taller than the tree,

55
00:03:03,563 --> 00:03:05,192
to prove their courage.

56
00:03:05,212 --> 00:03:10,495
Other accounts tell it differently,
but every Saturday from April to June,

57
00:03:10,515 --> 00:03:12,143
the dives still happen.

58
00:03:12,663 --> 00:03:17,143
Legend two, Roy Mata, a great
chief who died around 1600.

59
00:03:17,163 --> 00:03:19,117
On the island of Eretoka,

60
00:03:19,137 --> 00:03:24,486
archaeologists found one of the largest
mass burials in the Pacific.

61
00:03:25,006 --> 00:03:28,530
He is said to have drawn his last
breath in a cave on Lelepa island,

62
00:03:28,550 --> 00:03:31,813
and his domain became the first
World Heritage site in Vanuatu.

63
00:03:32,333 --> 00:03:33,372
And a mystery.

64
00:03:33,392 --> 00:03:38,588
In the 1930s, on Tanna, people began
to follow a man named John Frum.

65
00:03:38,608 --> 00:03:39,723
During the war,

66
00:03:39,743 --> 00:03:45,242
American troops arrived with more
goods than the islanders had ever seen.

67
00:03:45,762 --> 00:03:50,107
Followers say John Frum came
from America, and every February 15th,

68
00:03:50,127 --> 00:03:53,950
they wait for his return,
with food, vehicles and medicine.

69
00:03:54,470 --> 00:03:56,128
Nobody knows who he was.

70
00:03:56,148 --> 00:03:57,596
To some, he is white.

71
00:03:57,616 --> 00:03:59,205
To others, he is black.

72
00:03:59,225 --> 00:04:01,372
And he still has not come back.

73
00:04:01,892 --> 00:04:02,876
That was Vanuatu.

74
00:04:02,896 --> 00:04:04,942
Which country should we visit next?

75
00:04:04,962 --> 00:04:06,359
Tell me in the comments.

